      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Torsion of a normal ovary is difficult to diagnose. This usually leads to a delayed treatment hesitating in hemorrhagic infarction and necrosis. We report here a case in a 40 days old girl detected at operation following a clinical and radiological picture of acute abdomen."},
